After a /cd, @path mentions, /add, /explain and --image now refuse files under the new directory's [directories] deny entries, the same way read_file already did. Before this, the file tools refused such a path while @path still sent its contents to the provider. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass, and it's committed as ddbb29f1.

What changed
• **src/commands_file_fence.rs:** `admit_for_add` checks the startup fence first, and its result and wording are unchanged. If the startup fence allows the path, it then asks the `/cd list using cd_denied_dir_refusal_with, the same check the file tools use, so symlinks are judged by where they point. A refusal from the /cd list ends with (a [directories] deny entry applied by /cd), so you can tell it apart from a --deny-dir refusal. If /cd` hasn't added anything, nothing extra is checked.
• **`src/cd_config_note.rs:** added cd_denied_dirs_handle(), an 8-line function that hands out the session-wide list. It mirrors cd_deny::cd_added_deny_handle`.
• **How tests reach the list:** the functions behind the four doors have 47 callers across four files, so passing the list through all of them wasn't worth it. Tests call `admit_for_add_with(list, …) directly, or use a test-only per-thread override, TEST_CD_DIR_DENY`. No test touches the real session-wide list.

Tests: 6 new ones in src/commands_file_fence_tests.rs. The original 12 were not edited and still pass.
• **Refusals:** a direct path and a symlink are both refused, checked against the exact warning line. The `@`-mention, `/add`, `/explain` and `--image` doors each have a test. The mention test also confirms the same mention does get inlined when the /cd list is empty.
• **Both fences deny:** the startup fence's message is the one shown.
• **No change when unused:** with an empty /cd list, or one naming an unrelated folder, mention, /add and read output are byte-identical to before.
• **Sabotage check:** I disabled the new `/cd` check and re-ran the tests in one step. Exactly the 3 refusal tests failed and the other 15 passed. After restoring it, all 18 pass and the temporary NEUTERED marker is gone.

Still not done: 5 of the 6 measured file-path readers still see only the startup fence. They are:
• the context.rs loaders
• `commands_project.rs`
• `commands_rename.rs`
• `commands_map.rs`
• `commands_goal.rs`

[directories] allow, [permissions] allow, hooks, MCP servers and skills are also still not reloaded on /cd. This is written in the commit message, in a new section of ARCHITECTURE.md, and in a [comment on #869](https://github.com/yologdev/yoyo-evolve/issues/869#issuecomment-6116627654), which is still open. docs/src/configuration/permissions.md now lists these four doors as covered and names the readers that still aren't.
